From 4afe56fa8c3ad3dc64636b2aad09d22a476bf8ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fafwa <gsnchongus@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:52:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Drafted area kinds: one pure module draws a new kind in the
 game and the preview

A drafted kind (DraftedTypes) is a pure module in systems/drafted, listed in
systems/DraftedKinds and named by a DrawnEffects.area row of kind Drafted.
AreaFx and areapreview draw any such module the same generic way, so a new
kind needs no drawing code of its own. DraftedKinds.spec holds every one to
the contract: fixed count and shapes at every age and power, within the cast
budget, near the area, gone by its end, deterministic. ShardBloom is the
reference kind (row ShardBloomExample, spare).

Prototype from swarm-lab for the kind-drafting lane.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LSf2LshVSQPbhUqwjQ2h1n
